  "notes": "{騙|だま}す implies intentional deception to gain advantage or cause harm.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: {人|ひと}を{騙|だま}す\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {人|ひと}を{騙|だま}す: to deceive someone\n- {騙|だま}されないで: don't be fooled\n- うまく{騙|だま}す: to trick cleverly\n- {金|かね}を{騙|だま}し{取|と}る: to swindle money\n\nPASSIVE FORM:\n{騙|だま}される is very common, meaning \"to be deceived\" or \"to fall for a trick.\"\n\nRELATED:\n- {詐欺|さぎ}: fraud, scam\n- {嘘|うそ}をつく: to tell a lie (less malicious)\n- {欺|あざむ}く: to deceive (literary)",
